## 📌 Project Overview

Credit card fraud is a major challenge in digital financial transactions. 
Fraudulent transactions are usually very small compared with genuine transactions, 
which makes fraud detection a highly imbalanced classification problem.

This project develops a Machine Learning-based system to classify credit card 
transactions as **Genuine** or **Fraudulent**.

The project follows a complete Data Science workflow including:

- Data preprocessing
- Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
- Feature scaling
- Imbalanced data handling using SMOTE
- Machine Learning classification
- Model evaluation
- Feature importance analysis
- Fraud prediction

---

## 🎯 Objectives

The main objectives of this project are:

- Analyze credit card transaction data
- Understand patterns in fraudulent transactions
- Perform data cleaning and preprocessing
- Handle highly imbalanced transaction data
- Apply SMOTE to balance the training data
- Build classification models
- Compare different Machine Learning algorithms
- Evaluate models using multiple performance metrics
- Predict whether a transaction is genuine or fraudulent

